  "articleBody": "Getting clean, lasting paint on garage walls and ceilings depends entirely on correct preparation. Watch out for these common missteps: 1. Painting over grease and motor oil — Paint cannot adhere to vehicle residues or oily fingerprints without chemical degreasing. 2. Skipping dedicated primer — Bare drywall patches, raw masonry, or stained surfaces bleed through quickly if unsealed. 3. Using standard interior wall paint on high-abuse zones — High-wear areas need tough, washable sheens and coatings formulated to resist moisture and scuffs. 4. Applying coatings in poor temperatures — Cooler Colorado mornings can prevent coatings from curing, resulting in tacky or failing finishes. 5. Closing garage doors too soon — Trapping solvent or water vapors without adequate airflow leads to poor bonding and lingering odors. 6. Disturbing pre-1978 coatings unsafely — Older painted surfaces require certified lead-safe practices to contain harmful dust. What to Expect During the Process: Professional painters spend significant time scraping, patching, and cleaning before opening a paint can. HH Remodeling LLC delivers detailed drywall patching and painting to ensure long-term durability. Reach out at 303-505-0866 to review your project.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
